          Asphalt is the cheaper driveway to install and the more expensive one to own. Neither half of that sentence is a criticism — it is simply the trade you are making, and the quotes in front of you only show you the first half.
        </p>

        <h2 id="at-a-glance" class="scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
          1. Asphalt Driveway Cost at a Glance
        </h2>

        <p>
          A new asphalt driveway generally runs <strong>$4 to $10 per square foot installed</strong> in most US markets, with simple jobs in low-cost regions coming in closer to $3. That covers excavation, a compacted aggregate base, the hot mix itself, laying and rolling. Demolition of an existing surface is normally quoted separately.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
